    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "b69e9f05",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b69e9f05"
      },
      "source": [
        "*Two variables, 'Gender' and 'Smoking history' to be encoded*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "a495ad57",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "a495ad57"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Split data into train and test"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 16,
      "id": "7087df9a",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7087df9a"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X, y, test_size=0.3, random_state=42, stratify=y)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 17,
      "id": "502b31bc",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "502b31bc",
        "outputId": "63f09c72-366b-4f89-b509-0469a369ab5c"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "(67289, 8)\n",
            "(28839, 8)\n",
            "diabetes\n",
            "0    0.911769\n",
            "1    0.088231\n",
            "Name: proportion, dtype: float64\n",
            "diabetes\n",
            "0    0.911751\n",
            "1    0.088249\n",
            "Name: proportion, dtype: float64\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# check on split data\n",
        "\n",
        "print(X_train.shape)\n",
        "print(X_test.shape)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(y_train.value_counts(normalize=True))\n",
        "print(y_test.value_counts(normalize=True))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "6dba7f03",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6dba7f03"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Separate feature types"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 18,
      "id": "a2f2a1ab",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "a2f2a1ab"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "categorical_features = [\"gender\", \"smoking_history\"]\n",
        "numerical_features = [\"age\", \"hypertension\", \"heart_disease\", \"bmi\", \"HbA1c_level\", \"blood_glucose_level\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "7ca470d2",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7ca470d2"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Logistic Regression Model\n",
        "------\n",
        "(Baseline Model)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "07931d3f",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "07931d3f"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Preprocessing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 19,
      "id": "c581a2c0",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c581a2c0"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "preprocessor = ColumnTransformer(\n",
        "    transformers=[\n",
        "        (\"num\", StandardScaler(), numerical_features),\n",
        "        (\"cat\", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\"ignore\"), categorical_features)\n",
        "    ]\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "71867b8e",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "71867b8e"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Logistic Regression pipeline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 20,
      "id": "9a006066",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9a006066"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "log_reg = Pipeline([\n",
        "    (\"preprocessor\", preprocessor),\n",
        "    (\"model\", LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000))\n",
        "])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "574f5607",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "574f5607"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Training and prediction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 21,
      "id": "5c129cc4",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5c129cc4"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "log_reg.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "y_pred = log_reg.predict(X_test)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "30dc1937",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "30dc1937"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Accuracy check"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 22,
      "id": "72ccde4e",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "72ccde4e",
        "outputId": "ec385ad5-aa98-43ba-f49a-66b5c55d8408"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Accuracy: 0.9575227989874823\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "accuracy = accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred)\n",
        "print(\"Accuracy:\", accuracy)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "58832d5c",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "58832d5c"
      },
      "source": [
        "*A higher accuracy in this case does not necessarily indicate that the model performs well, due to the substantial class imbalance between diabetic and non-diabetic observations. Since the majority class consists of non-diabetic observations, the model can achieve relatively high accuracy by predicting more observations as non-diabetic, while potentially failing to correctly identify diabetic cases.*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 23,
      "id": "a8be6d97",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "a8be6d97",
        "outputId": "a6ac995a-f745-4213-d6c0-7990a3248330"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[[26006   288]\n",
            " [  937  1608]]\n",
            "              precision    recall  f1-score   support\n",
            "\n",
            "           0       0.97      0.99      0.98     26294\n",
            "           1       0.85      0.63      0.72      2545\n",
            "\n",
            "    accuracy                           0.96     28839\n",
            "   macro avg       0.91      0.81      0.85     28839\n",
            "weighted avg       0.95      0.96      0.95     28839\n",
            "\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Confusion matrix\n",
        "\n",
        "cm = confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred)\n",
        "print(cm)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Classification report\n",
        "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "efcc2ec4",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "efcc2ec4"
      },
      "source": [
        "*The baseline Logistic Regression model distinguishes non-diabetic cases very well, but its ability to detect diabetic cases is substantially weaker, with 63% recall.*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "25bb7a99",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "25bb7a99"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Handling class imbalance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "456664f1",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "456664f1"
      },
      "source": [
        "(Balanced Logistic Regression model)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 24,
      "id": "54926c68",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "54926c68"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "log_reg_balanced = Pipeline([\n",
        "    (\"preprocessor\", preprocessor),\n",
        "    (\"model\", LogisticRegression(\n",
        "        class_weight={0: 1, 1: 3},\n",
        "        max_iter=1000\n",
        "    ))\n",
        "])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 25,
      "id": "3534a868",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3534a868"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "log_reg_balanced.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "y_pred = log_reg_balanced.predict(X_test)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 26,
      "id": "e31aed2a",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "e31aed2a",
        "outputId": "bd83ea41-10b9-4cb0-88e1-c73c883befbc"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            " Accuracy: 0.9414334755019245\n",
            " Confusion matrix: \n",
            "[[25252  1042]\n",
            " [  647  1898]]\n",
            " Classification report: \n",
            "              precision    recall  f1-score   support\n",
            "\n",
            "           0       0.98      0.96      0.97     26294\n",
            "           1       0.65      0.75      0.69      2545\n",
            "\n",
            "    accuracy                           0.94     28839\n",
            "   macro avg       0.81      0.85      0.83     28839\n",
            "weighted avg       0.95      0.94      0.94     28839\n",
            "\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def report (y_test, y_pred):\n",
        "    accuracy = accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred)\n",
        "    cm = confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred)\n",
        "    class_report = classification_report(y_test, y_pred)\n",
        "    print(f\" Accuracy: {accuracy}\\n Confusion matrix: \\n{cm}\\n Classification report: \\n{class_report}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "report(y_test, y_pred)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "7fc6e015",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7fc6e015"
      },
      "source": [
        "*class_weight=\"balanced\", and manually tuned class weight substantially increased the model's ability to detect class 1, but it also produced many more false positives.*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "7c1eaca3",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7c1eaca3"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Random Forest Classifier\n",
        "------\n",
        "(Baseline Model)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "bc5eedb2",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "bc5eedb2"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Preprocessing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 27,
      "id": "4451b0ce",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4451b0ce"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "rf_preprocessor = ColumnTransformer(\n",
        "    transformers=[\n",
        "        (\"cat\", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\"ignore\"), categorical_features)\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    remainder=\"passthrough\"\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "4c2757b0",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4c2757b0"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Random Forest pipeline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 28,
      "id": "7d4e5937",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7d4e5937"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "random_forest = Pipeline([\n",
        "    (\"preprocessor\", rf_preprocessor),\n",
        "    (\"model\", RandomForestClassifier(\n",
        "        n_estimators=100,\n",
        "        random_state=42\n",
        "    ))\n",
        "])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "af32803d",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "af32803d"
      },
      "source": [
        "* Train and Predict"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 29,
      "id": "db936515",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "db936515"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "random_forest.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "y_pred = random_forest.predict(X_test)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 30,
      "id": "0ae26d4f",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "0ae26d4f",
        "outputId": "a0a05023-6d3f-4883-b1bd-6711e23d97bd"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            " Accuracy: 0.9690696626096605\n",
            " Confusion matrix: \n",
            "[[26197    97]\n",
            " [  795  1750]]\n",
            " Classification report: \n",
            "              precision    recall  f1-score   support\n",
            "\n",
            "           0       0.97      1.00      0.98     26294\n",
            "           1       0.95      0.69      0.80      2545\n",
            "\n",
            "    accuracy                           0.97     28839\n",
            "   macro avg       0.96      0.84      0.89     28839\n",
            "weighted avg       0.97      0.97      0.97     28839\n",
            "\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "report(y_test, y_pred)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "5bd37d8b",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5bd37d8b"
      },
      "source": [
        "*The baseline Random Forest has lower diabetic recall than the class-weighted Logistic Regression, despite having higher accuracy and F1.*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "a6a7a084",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "a6a7a084"
      },
      "source": [
        "(Balanced Random Forest Model)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 31,
      "id": "20456d56",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "20456d56"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "random_forest_balanced = Pipeline([\n",
        "    (\"preprocessor\", preprocessor),\n",
        "    (\"model\", RandomForestClassifier(\n",
        "        class_weight={0: 1, 1: 3},\n",
        "        n_estimators=100,\n",
        "        random_state=42\n",
        "    ))\n",
        "])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 32,
      "id": "56d26ebd",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "56d26ebd"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "random_forest_balanced.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "y_pred = random_forest_balanced.predict(X_test)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 33,
      "id": "fe2a9944",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "fe2a9944",
        "outputId": "15ab5318-45f2-4e24-9e0c-1255f5acaab4"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            " Accuracy: 0.9683761572870072\n",
            " Confusion matrix: \n",
            "[[26178   116]\n",
            " [  796  1749]]\n",
            " Classification report: \n",
            "              precision    recall  f1-score   support\n",
            "\n",
            "           0       0.97      1.00      0.98     26294\n",
